The compiler is now destiny, and Phobos is now Fate

The language is called Destiny, and its compiler is called `destiny`.

$(UL
$(LI The build produces a binary named `destiny` (`destiny.exe` on
Windows) instead of `dmd`.)
$(LI The compiler reads its settings from `destiny.conf` instead of
`dmd.conf`. On Windows the file is still `sc.ini`. Rename an existing
`dmd.conf` to keep using it.)
$(LI `destiny --version` prints `Destiny64 Compiler` (or `Destiny32`)
instead of `DMD64 D Compiler`.)
$(LI The standard library, previously Phobos, is called Fate. It is
expected in the sibling folder `../fate`, and is cloned from
`https://github.com/Destiny-Org/fate` when missing. Its modules are still
named `std.*`.)
)

Removed from the repository:

$(UL
$(LI CI configurations for services Destiny does not use: Azure
Pipelines, CircleCI and Codecov.)
$(LI The dlang nightly, release and performance workflows.)
$(LI `CODEOWNERS`, which listed upstream maintainers.)
$(LI The deprecated `posix.mak` files and the `src/` compatibility
directory. Use the top-level `Makefile`.)
)
